From: Chu Qinghao <6337103+qinghao1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11/17] bridge: silence refresh-rate probe error in headless

The headless WASM build has no display by design (Noop renderer, input
via VpxWasm_PushKey, host-driven via VpxWasm_StepFrame), so the SDL
refresh-rate probe in Window::Window always yields 0Hz and the ERROR
log is spurious. The 60Hz fallback value is still assigned as the
fixed step rate; only the log is suppressed, and only under
VPX_HEADLESS_BRIDGE. Desktop behavior is unchanged.

diff --git a/src/renderer/Window.cpp b/src/renderer/Window.cpp
index 95da8d0f..f5198b9b 100644
--- a/src/renderer/Window.cpp
+++ b/src/renderer/Window.cpp
@@ -172,7 +172,13 @@ Window::Window(const string& title, const Settings& settings, VPXWindowId window
 
    if (m_refreshrate <= 0)
    {
+#ifdef VPX_HEADLESS_BRIDGE
+      // Headless WASM has no display by design (Noop renderer, host-driven via
+      // VpxWasm_StepFrame), so a 0Hz SDL probe is expected: silently keep the
+      // fixed 60Hz step rate instead of logging a spurious ERROR.
+#else
       PLOGE << "Failed to get display refresh rate. VPX will use a 60Hz default which may be wrong and cause bad video synchronization.";
+#endif
       m_refreshrate = 60;
    }
 
